Implement user story AMSD-1820: [Mozio] - Fix promo code discount amount display for return trip in email confirmation

## Story Description
When a return trip ticket with a promo code is purchased, the Mozio email confirmation fails to display the promo code discount amount for the return trip line item. The outbound trip discount displays correctly, but the return trip discount is either missing or rendered incorrectly. This story fixes the email confirmation template to consistently display promo code discount amounts for both outbound and return trip line items, matching the discount values recorded in the order payload.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Given a return trip ticket with a promo code is purchased, the Mozio email confirmation displays the promo code discount amount for the outbound trip line item.
- Given a return trip ticket with a promo code is purchased, the Mozio email confirmation displays the promo code discount amount for the return trip line item.
- The promo code discount amount shown for the return trip in the email confirmation equals the discount value applied to the return portion of the order as recorded in the order payload.
- Given multiple line items share the same date range and a promo code is applied, the Mozio email confirmation displays the promo code discount amount for both outbound and return trip line items.
- Given no promo code is applied to the order, the Mozio email confirmation does not display a promo code discount amount for either the outbound or return trip line item.
- Given the promo code discount value for the return portion is zero, the Mozio email confirmation displays a discount amount of zero for the return trip without omitting the discount line.
- The promo code discount amount for the return trip is rendered in the same currency format (symbol placement, decimal precision) and same relative position within the return line item section as the outbound trip discount appears within the outbound line item section in the Mozio email confirmation.
- Given the promo code discount amount for the return trip includes a fractional currency value, the Mozio email confirmation displays the discount with the correct number of decimal places matching the currency's standard format.
- Given the order payload contains a promo code discount for the return trip with a negative or unexpectedly large value, the email confirmation renders the discount amount as recorded in the order payload without silently suppressing or modifying it.
- Given the email confirmation is viewed in a text-only email client, the promo code discount amount for the return trip remains readable and correctly surfaced alongside the return trip line item.
- Given a promo code applies only to the outbound portion of a return trip order (return discount is absent from the order payload), the Mozio email confirmation does not display a promo code discount line for the return trip.





